---
import HomeLayout from '../../layouts/HomeLayout.astro';
import { modernReviews } from '../../data/review-registry';
import '../../styles/review.css';
import '../../styles/beans.css';
import '../../styles/bean-guides.css';

const date = '2026-10-27';
const path = '/grinder/best-compact-electric-espresso-grinders/';
const canonical = 'https://coffeedant.com' + path;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const local = (p: string) => base + p.replace(/^\//, '');
const title = 'Best Compact Electric Espresso Grinders';
const description = 'Three exact US electric espresso grinders compared by manufacturer footprint, counter clearance, dosing access, cleaning and independent use evidence.';
const specs = [
  {slug:'/grinder/fellow-opus-2/', best:'Lowest published height', width:130, depth:206, height:267, workflow:'Weigh each dose; use the supplied espresso cup', tradeoff:'The plastic grind path and filter-cup results in an independent sample are real compromises', skip:'You need a hopper left full or a metal-heavy build', evidence:'Fellow publishes a 130 × 206 × 267 mm body and a single-dose workflow. The Coffee Chronicler found tidy espresso use on one sample, while criticizing plastic internal parts and weaker filter results. [1] [4]'},
  {slug:'/grinder/baratza-encore-esp-pro/', best:'Shallowest published body', width:130, depth:150, height:340, workflow:'Choose timed hopper dosing or single dosing', tradeoff:'The tall hopper and top collar need usable space above the cabinet line', skip:'Your cabinet clearance is tight or you want the simplest burr removal', evidence:'Baratza specifies 130 × 150 × 340 mm. Expert Reviews found its sample versatile but reported an unreliable empty-hopper auto-stop and difficult first cleaning. Its UK sample experience is context, not a US-unit reliability rate. [2] [5]'},
  {slug:'/grinder/eureka-mignon-zero-65-all-purpose/', best:'Narrow stepless upgrade', width:133, depth:215, height:357, workflow:'Single-dose into the cup or portafilter with bellows and marked dial', tradeoff:'Tallest and deepest of this shortlist; allow room for bellows and adjustment', skip:'You want a low-effort hopper routine or a guaranteed empty grind path', evidence:'Eureka publishes 133 × 215 × 357 mm, 65 mm flat burrs and a revolution-counting dial. Kaffeemacher found nonzero retained grounds under its own protocol; the marketing name is not a cleanliness guarantee. [3] [6]'}
];
const picks = specs.map(p => ({...p, review: modernReviews.find(r => r.slug === p.slug)!}));
if (picks.some(p => !p.review)) throw new Error('Compact grinder guide references an unregistered review');
const sections = [
  {id:'selection', title:'Measure the space you actually use', paragraphs:[
    'This shortlist solves a physical fit problem: fitting an electric espresso-capable grinder beside a machine and still reaching its controls, beans and cleaning parts. We included only exact reviewed models with current manufacturer width, depth and height data, a US configuration, and enough independent use evidence to discuss a limitation. We excluded grinders with missing comparable dimensions or a larger body that did not improve this particular decision. The dimensions are manufacturer body specifications, not measurements taken by Coffeedant. [1] [2] [3]',
    'Measure the countertop from backsplash to usable front edge, then the gap from counter to cabinet underside. Reserve room around the grinder for a cup or portafilter, a hand on the adjustment, its power cord, and safe access to remove beans and clean the burr chamber. A body that fits exactly on paper can be awkward under a low cupboard. None of the three published dimensions proves that the top-opening or bellows can operate within the same height. Make a cardboard rectangle for the footprint before ordering.'
  ]},
  {id:'footprint', title:'A smaller footprint can still have a worse reach', paragraphs:[
    'The three bodies are all narrow, at 130–133 mm wide, but their proportions differ. The Encore ESP Pro is the shallowest on the stated dimensions at 150 mm deep; it is 340 mm tall and its hopper or single-dose lid and adjustment collar are above the body. Opus 2 is 267 mm tall, yet 206 mm deep. The Zero 65 All Purpose is 357 mm tall and 215 mm deep, before any practical clearance for its bellows. Those figures are useful for screening a shelf, not a complete installed-space drawing. [1] [2] [3]',
    'Counter placement also determines which control feels convenient. Opus 2 uses a side adjustment dial; check which side remains reachable next to your espresso machine. The Baratza changes grind at the upper collar and presents a front display. Eureka has a large marked dial and a dosing fork, but the bellows needs space above. A tight counter can make the theoretically smaller grinder harder to use if the accessible side faces a wall.'
  ]},
  {id:'workflow', title:'Choose the dose routine before the dimensions', paragraphs:[
    'Opus 2 is the most natural fit for someone who weighs a fresh dose for every espresso and sometimes grinds filter coffee. Fellow supplies two magnetic catch cups and describes the espresso cup as compatible with 54 mm and 58 mm portafilters. That is a cup-transfer statement, not universal portafilter fit: different baskets, handles and funnels still matter. Its one stepless dial removes the older Opus inner-ring routine. The Coffee Chronicler liked its speed and low mess on a particular sample, but found its plastic grind chamber and filter cup less convincing. [1] [4]',
    'The Encore ESP Pro can keep beans in a hopper for timed doses or run a single-dose mode. That flexibility matters in a cramped shared kitchen where weighing every serving may be impractical. The independent Expert Reviews sample worked across espresso and filter, but its empty-hopper stop sometimes required a manual stop, and initial disassembly was awkward. Do not infer a failure frequency for every unit from one reviewer. Check that the collar can be reached and the hopper removed in your actual cabinet gap. [2] [5]',
    'The Eureka Zero 65 All Purpose is the specialist choice for a narrow station where careful espresso adjustment and occasional brewing changes justify a bellows routine. Its 65 mm flat burrs, stepless micrometric setting and revolution counter are exact-model features. The bellows can help clear loose grounds, yet independent Kaffeemacher measurements show that “Zero” is not literal empty retention. The substantial 5.6 kg body also makes frequent lifting to clear a cabinet less attractive. [3] [6]'
  ]},
  {id:'maintenance', title:'Leave enough room to keep it clean', paragraphs:[
    'All three need access for periodic cleaning. A grinder pushed hard against a backsplash or trapped under a fixed shelf invites skipped maintenance, especially when the hopper or burr assembly must come off. Follow the exact manual, unplug first, and keep water away from electrical and burr components unless that manual explicitly permits it. A brush, bellows or anti-static feature reduces a particular mess; none replaces scheduled cleaning. [7] [8] [9]',
    'The Encore ESP Pro’s independent disassembly difficulty deserves weight if hand strength or access is limited. Fellow describes tool-free burr access, which is convenient on paper, while its plastic chamber is a material tradeoff. Eureka’s bellows and cup add steps to the morning routine. Plan space for the accessories as well as the body; a compact machine surrounded by loose cups and funnels is not a compact station. [1] [3] [5]'
  ]},
  {id:'value', title:'Compare the whole station, not a dated sticker price', paragraphs:[
    'We did not verify one comparable delivered US checkout total for the exact selected colors and voltages on October 26, so this guide does not rank current prices or discounts. The linked full reviews contain dated offer context; recheck a legitimate US seller, taxes, shipping, stock and return terms before purchase. None of these models should be substituted with an older Opus, Encore ESP or Mignon Zero 55 merely because a retailer shortens the name. [1] [2] [3]',
    'A shallow grinder may let you retain a usable prep zone, while a shorter body may fit a cabinet. Either saving is valuable only if the grind quality and daily routine meet your espresso needs. Keep room in the setup budget for a scale, a compatible cup or funnel, and a sensible cleaning kit. Avoid buying a larger hopper or dosing accessory until the body has been placed and used. For a travel kit or a counter with no safe electrical space, the separate reviewed K-Ultra hand grinder may be a better category entirely, with hand effort as its explicit cost.'
  ]}
];
const faqs = [
  {q:'Which is shortest under a cabinet?', a:'Fellow lists Opus 2 at 267 mm high, versus 340 mm for Encore ESP Pro and 357 mm for Zero 65 All Purpose. Leave extra room for loading and servicing; body height alone is insufficient.'},
  {q:'Which uses the least published counter depth?', a:'Baratza lists the Encore ESP Pro at 150 mm deep, versus 206 mm for Opus 2 and 215 mm for Eureka Zero 65 All Purpose. Leave front space for the catch cup or portafilter.'},
  {q:'Are these measurements Coffeedant measurements?', a:'No. They are manufacturer dimensions for the exact named models, checked October 26, 2026. Check the selected US variant and any accessories against your own space.'},
  {q:'Can all three grind for espresso?', a:'Yes, their makers specify espresso-capable adjustment. Actual basket, beans and recipe determine the setting; the guide does not claim a side-by-side taste result.'},
  {q:'Does the Eureka bellows leave zero coffee inside?', a:'No. The independent sample study found nonzero retained coffee under its protocol. A bellows helps a workflow but does not prove a completely empty path.'},
  {q:'Can I keep the Baratza hopper under a low cabinet?', a:'Only if there is room to load beans, turn the collar and remove parts for cleaning. Measure the clearance in your kitchen beyond the published 340 mm body height.'},
  {q:'Are these current US price rankings?', a:'No. This guide uses no unverified numeric price or discount. Confirm the exact finish, voltage, availability and delivered total in the live US cart.'}
];
const sources = [
  ['Fellow: Opus 2 US product', 'https://fellowproducts.com/products/opus-2-conical-burr-grinder', 'Exact generation, dimensions, dosing cups, adjustment and maintenance claims.'],
  ['Baratza: Encore ESP Pro specifications', 'https://www.baratza.com/en-ca/product/encore-esp-pro-zcg595', 'Exact ZCG595 model dimensions and dosing modes; US listing checked separately for market identity.'],
  ['Eureka: Mignon Zero 65 All Purpose', 'https://www.eureka.co.it/en/products/eureka%2B1920/prosumer%2Bgrinders/zero%2Brange/118/', 'Exact dimensions, weight, burr, dial, bellows and fork specifications.'],
  ['The Coffee Chronicler: Opus 2 sample review', 'https://coffeechronicler.com/fellow-opus-2-review/', 'Independent September 2026 sample, workflow and material limitations; not a universal result.'],
  ['Expert Reviews: Encore ESP Pro sample', 'https://www.expertreviews.co.uk/home-garden/small-appliances/coffee-machines/baratza-encore-esp-pro-review', 'Independent UK sample of the exact model; stop and cleaning observations are bounded.'],
  ['Kaffeemacher: Eureka Zero 65 AP comparison', 'https://kaffeemacher.de/en/blogs/kaffeewissen/eureka-zero-vergleichstest', 'Independent sample measurements and nonzero-retention context.'],
  ['Fellow: Opus 2 safety manual', 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0057/6235/1219/files/Fellow_Opus2_SafetyManual_789-00291_F.pdf?v=1777654475', 'Exact-generation cleaning and safety instructions.'],
  ['Baratza: manuals and documentation', 'https://www.baratza.com/en-us/documents', 'Encore ESP Pro manual entry and service context.'],
  ['Eureka: exact-model manual link', 'https://www.eureka.co.it/en/products/eureka%2B1920/prosumer%2Bgrinders/zero%2Brange/118/', 'Manufacturer manual link and model-specific care context.'],
  ['Baratza: Encore ESP Pro US listing', 'https://www.baratza.com/en-us/product/encore-esp-pro-zcg595', 'US-market product identity and current availability context, without a quoted offer.']
];
const cite = (p: string) => p.replace(/\[(\d+)\]/g, (_m,n) => '<a class="bean-cite" href="#s' + n + '" aria-label="Source ' + n + '">[' + n + ']</a>');
const author = {'@type':'Person',name:'Aleksandar Spasevski',jobTitle:'Editor, Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/about/',image:'https://coffeedant.com/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg'};
const schema = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@graph':[
  {'@type':'Article','@id':canonical+'#article',headline:title,description,genre:'Research-led grinder buying guide',inLanguage:'en-US',datePublished:date,dateModified:date,author,mainEntityOfPage:canonical,image:picks.map(p=>p.review.image),citation:sources.map(s=>s[1]),publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/'}},
  {'@type':'ItemList','@id':canonical+'#shortlist',name:title,itemListElement:picks.map((p,i)=>({'@type':'ListItem',position:i+1,name:p.review.brand+' '+p.review.model,url:'https://coffeedant.com'+p.slug}))},
  {'@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:'https://coffeedant.com/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'Grinders',item:'https://coffeedant.com/grinder/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:3,name:title,item:canonical}]},
  {'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faqs.map(f=>({'@type':'Question',name:f.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:f.a}}))}
]};
---
<HomeLayout title={title+' | Coffeedant'} description={description} canonicalPath={path} image={picks[0].review.image} imageAlt={picks[0].review.imageAlt} ogType="article" published={date} updated={date}>
  <main id="main-content" class="review-page bean-buying-guide" data-guide-kind="grinders">
    <div class="review-shell">
      <nav class="review-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Home</a><span>/</span><a href={local('/grinder/')}>Grinders</a><span>/</span><span>Compact electric</span></nav>
      <header class="bean-guide-header"><p class="review-overline">Grinder buying guide · research-led · United States</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="bean-lead">Three narrow grinders solve different counter problems. Check depth, cabinet clearance and the room your hands need before choosing by body size.</p><aside class="review-author-card"><div class="review-author-head"><img src={local('/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg')} alt="Aleksandar Spasevski, editor at Coffeedant" width="46" height="46" /><div><strong>Aleksandar Spasevski</strong><small>Editor, Coffeedant</small></div></div><p>Published <time datetime={date}>October 27, 2026</time> · Sources checked October 26–27 · US product context</p><p>I compared current manufacturer dimensions and exact-model documents with independent sample reviews. Coffeedant has not handled, ground, measured or tasted with these grinders. The picks are research-led space and workflow judgments.</p></aside></header>
      <nav class="bean-jump" aria-label="Guide sections"><strong>Plan your counter</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={'#'+s.id}>{s.title}</a>)}<a href="#quick-compare">Comparison</a><a href="#picks">The picks</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
      <article class="bean-article">
        {sections.slice(0,2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">The space decision</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="quick-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Manufacturer body dimensions</p><h2>Quick comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable compact espresso grinder comparison"><table><caption>Width × depth × height in millimeters; clearance for loading and cleaning is additional</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Exact grinder</th><th scope="col">Body</th><th scope="col">Best fit</th><th scope="col">Main limit</th></tr></thead><tbody>{picks.map(p=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.brand} {p.review.model}</a></th><td>{p.width} × {p.depth} × {p.height} mm</td><td>{p.best}</td><td>{p.tradeoff}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="picks"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Exact US model identities</p><h2>Three defensible picks</h2></header><div class="bean-index-grid">{picks.map(p=><article class="bean-guide-pick"><img src={p.review.image} alt={p.review.imageAlt} width="360" height="360" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div><p class="review-overline">{p.best}</p><h3><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.brand} {p.review.model}</a></h3><p><strong>Evidence:</strong> <span set:html={cite(p.evidence)} /></p><p><strong>Daily routine:</strong> {p.workflow}.</p><p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> {p.tradeoff}.</p><p><strong>Skip if:</strong> {p.skip}.</p><p class="bean-credit"><a href={p.review.links[0]?.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Image and product: {p.review.brand}</a>. Manufacturer or seller media for identification; no Coffeedant test photo.</p><a class="bean-guide-review-link" href={local(p.slug)}>Read the full review →</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="detailed-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">More than body width</p><h2>Detailed comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable detailed compact grinder comparison"><table><caption>Documented form factors and research-led fit; no Coffeedant performance ranking</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Factor</th>{picks.map(p=><th scope="col"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.model}</a></th>)}</tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Width</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.width} mm</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Depth</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.depth} mm</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Body height</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.height} mm</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Dose routine</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.workflow}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Reason to skip</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.skip}</td>)}</tr></tbody></table></div></section>
        {sections.slice(2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Live with the grinder</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="related"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Related decisions</p><h2>Explore the rest of the station</h2></header><div class="bean-alternatives"><a href={local('/grinder/')}><strong>All grinder reviews</strong><span>See electric and manual alternatives outside this footprint shortlist.</span></a><a href={local('/grinder/best-grinders-for-switching-regular-and-decaf/')}><strong>Regular and decaf grinder guide</strong><span>Choose a routine for two beans without assuming zero carryover.</span></a><a href={local('/espresso-machine/small/')}><strong>Small espresso machines</strong><span>Reserve counter space for both the machine and grinder.</span></a></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="methodology"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Evidence and limits</p><h2>How this guide was made</h2></header><div class="review-section-body"><p>We screened the existing Coffeedant grinder reviews for exact electric models sold for espresso with current manufacturer width, depth and height specifications. These three offer distinct physical and dosing choices. We compared published controls and independent sample findings, then kept each sample observation within its own test context. We did not calculate a counter-area winner as a proxy for espresso quality.</p><p>Sources were checked October 26, 2026. There is no Coffeedant hands-on test, sound measurement, retention measurement, taste comparison or verified delivered-price ranking here. Product images are credited identification media. The reader should check the actual US variant and measure installed clearance before ordering; affiliate links in full reviews do not control the selection.</p></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="faq"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Quick answers</p><h2>Compact grinder FAQ</h2></header><div class="bean-faq">{faqs.map(f=><article><h3>{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="sources"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Trace the claims</p><h2>Sources</h2></header><ol class="review-source-list">{sources.map((s,i)=><li id={'s'+(i+1)}><a href={s[1]} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{s[0]} ↗</a><p>{s[2]} Checked October 26, 2026.</p></li>)}</ol></section>
        <section class="final-verdict"><p class="review-overline">The practical choice</p><h2>Fit the routine as well as the body</h2><p>Choose Opus 2 for the lowest stated body height, Encore ESP Pro for the shallowest body and hopper flexibility, or Zero 65 All Purpose for a narrow single-dose upgrade. Test the real loading, adjustment and cleaning clearances in your kitchen before buying.</p><a class="review-buy-button review-buy-button-dark" href={local('/grinder/')}>Explore all grinders →</a></section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema).replace(/</g,'\\u003c')} />
</HomeLayout>
